Contrail is an unofficial Telegram client and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Telegram FZ-LLC
or the Telegram Desktop project. Telegram is a trademark of Telegram FZ-LLC. It uses the Telegram API
with its own api_id, which every build must supply (see README.md).

It is built on TDLib (https://github.com/tdlib/td), Telegram's library for clients:
  Copyright Aliaksei Levin, Arseny Smirnov
  Licensed under the Boost Software License 1.0.
The build downloads TDLib at the commit pinned in build-env/build-tdlib.sh and compiles it in.

It uses parts of Telegram Desktop (https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop):
  Copyright John Preston and Telegram Desktop contributors
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3, with the OpenSSL exception.
These are the English interface strings, the call tones, the sound device module for calls and, from Telegram
Desktop's sources at its release tag, tgcalls (LGPL-3.0). For sound and video in calls the build also compiles
tg_owt (WebRTC, with the patch in patches/tg_owt/) and rnnoise at the versions the official Telegram Desktop
build uses.

The interface strings in other languages come from Telegram's translations, loaded through TDLib.
The application icon and the icons in gtk-ui/icons/ were made for Contrail.
